/*
=====================================================
LAYER 1 — WHAT THE SYSTEM ACTUALLY IS
=====================================================

At the most basic level, DVSM is a structured decision system.

It takes in information from the outside world and produces a
controlled, predictable response.

Every cycle follows the same loop:

1. Receive signals
2. Interpret meaning
3. Decide allowable action
4. Record outcome permanently

What matters here is not speed or intelligence,
but consistency.

Core idea:

    DVSM is not a predictive system.
    It is a resolution system.

It does not try to “guess the future.”
It ensures that given the same inputs,
the same outputs will always occur.

=====================================================
LAYER 2 — WHY INTERPRETATION COMES BEFORE ACTION
=====================================================

Most systems fail because they react too quickly.

They treat all incoming signals as equal,
and immediately respond.

DVSM explicitly avoids this.

Instead, it inserts a mandatory interpretation stage.

Every signal must first be understood in context:

- Is this a safety issue?
- Is this a stability issue?
- Or is this just an optimization concern?

This prevents low-priority signals from interfering
with critical system behavior.

Core idea:

    Understanding always comes before execution.

Nothing is acted on until its meaning is determined.

=====================================================
LAYER 3 — WHY EVERYTHING IS CLASSIFIED
=====================================================

Once signals are understood, they are grouped into categories.

This is not organizational — it is structural.

DVSM uses three fundamental strata:

1. Integrity
   → Rules that must never be violated
   → System safety constraints
   → Non-negotiable conditions

2. Stability
   → System health and consistency
   → Drift control and coherence maintenance

3. Energy
   → Performance, speed, and efficiency
   → Optimization space under safe conditions

This classification ensures that all system inputs
are not treated as equal “votes,” but as structured constraints.

Core idea:

    Not all inputs are allowed to influence decisions equally.

=====================================================
LAYER 4 — WHY ORDER OF IMPORTANCE IS FIXED
=====================================================

After classification, DVSM applies a strict ordering rule.

This ordering never changes, regardless of load, time, or context:

1. Integrity overrides everything
2. Stability overrides performance
3. Energy is only considered when safe

This prevents negotiation between incompatible concerns.

For example:

- The system will never sacrifice correctness for speed
- It will never ignore instability to save resources
- It will only optimize energy when the system is already safe

Core idea:

    DVSM does not “balance trade-offs.”
    It enforces hierarchy.

=====================================================
LAYER 5 — WHY THE LEDGER EXISTS
=====================================================

DVSM records every decision in a permanent ledger.

This ledger is:

- append-only (nothing is overwritten)
- fully reproducible
- fully auditable
- deterministic across replays

This creates a system memory that cannot drift or be altered.

It ensures that:

- past behavior is always reconstructable
- system evolution is transparent
- no hidden state changes can exist

Core idea:

    The system cannot rewrite its history.

It can only extend it.

=====================================================
LAYER 6 — HOW THE SYSTEM BEHAVES UNDER PRESSURE
=====================================================

Real systems are constrained by resources:

- CPU limits
- memory limits
- energy limits
- latency constraints

DVSM handles this without changing correctness.

Instead of breaking or mutating behavior,
it adjusts execution intensity.

This means:

- it can slow down processing
- it can defer non-critical operations
- it can reduce optimization depth

But critically:

- it never changes what is considered correct
- it never alters classification outcomes
- it never modifies arbitration rules

Core idea:

    Constraints affect speed, not truth.

=====================================================
LAYER 7 — WHY THE ENERGY LAYER EXISTS
=====================================================

The Energy Governance Boundary Layer (EGBL)
is the outermost control mechanism.

It is often misunderstood, so clarity is important:

It does NOT decide outcomes.

It only controls how much computation is used.

Think of it as a throttle:

- more energy → higher fidelity execution
- less energy → reduced computational depth

But in all cases:

- decisions remain identical
- logic remains identical
- correctness remains unchanged

Core idea:

    Energy affects execution cost, not system meaning.

=====================================================
LAYER 8 — WHY THIS SEPARATION IS IMPORTANT
=====================================================

Most systems fail when under stress because they
begin to change how they reason.

DVSM prevents this entirely by separation:

- Meaning is fixed (classification layer)
- Order is fixed (arbitration hierarchy)
- History is fixed (ledger)
- Execution speed is flexible (energy layer)

This separation ensures the system cannot “drift”
into inconsistent behavior.

Core idea:

    DVSM never adapts what is true.
    Only how fast truth is computed.

=====================================================
LAYER 9 — WHAT MAKES THIS DESIGN DIFFERENT
=====================================================

Traditional systems mix:

- decision logic
- optimization logic
- resource management

DVSM separates them completely.

This produces three guarantees:

1. Determinism
   → same input always produces same output

2. Auditability
   → every decision can be traced

3. Stability under load
   → system degrades gracefully without semantic change

Core idea:

    Complexity is allowed.
    Ambiguity is not.

=====================================================
LAYER 10 — FINAL INTUITION (EVERYDAY VERSION)
=====================================================

If simplified completely:

DVSM is a system that:

- understands before acting
- prioritizes safety over performance
- never forgets past decisions
- slows down under pressure without changing correctness

The energy system is not the “brain.”

It is just the control dial.

Core idea:

    DVSM is a truth-preserving system,
    not a performance-driven one.

